 "result": "Call order when a view raises (from `brain/request-lifecycle.md`):\n\n1. `Tessel.wsgi_entry` — `src/tessel/app.py`\n2. `run_full_request(ctx)` — `src/tessel/app.py` (catches the exception from `run_view`)\n3. `route_user_fault` — `src/tessel/app.py`\n4. `_pick_fault_handler` — `src/tessel/sansio/app.py` (chooses the registered handler)\n5. The chosen registered handler runs, or `route_http_fault` — `src/tessel/app.py` — for HTTP exceptions\n6. If nothing handles it, `route_unhandled_fault` — `src/tessel/app.py` (logs, sends `got_request_exception`, returns 500 or re-raises under `PROPAGATE_EXCEPTIONS`/debug)\n\nThe note doesn't say how `_pick_fault_handler` ranks handlers (for example bundle vs. app-level, or by exception class). Open `src/tessel/sansio/app.py` if you need that.",
